  "description": "The backward page TRANSITION: PF7 from page three of twenty-five records, resuming from CDEMO-CT00-TRNID-FIRST. PROCESS-PAGE-BACKWARD is the mirror of the forward path with four differences, and this case drives all four. The skip-read guard at :339 names a DIFFERENT key set - 'NOT DFHENTER AND DFHPF8' - so DFHPF7 does read, consuming record twenty-one, the anchor already shown as row one of page three. WS-IDX is primed at TEN by :349 and DECREMENTED by :355, so the ten records read in descending order - twenty down to eleven - land in screen rows ten down to one and the page reads in ascending order on the terminal. CDEMO-CT00-TRNID-LAST is therefore written FIRST (WS-IDX 10, record twenty) and CDEMO-CT00-TRNID-FIRST LAST (WS-IDX 1, record eleven). There is no look-ahead read; instead :360 reads once more, finds record ten, and because NEXT-PAGE-YES was set at :242 and the page number exceeds one, :364 SUBTRACTs one to give two. One send.",
